# The bulk of the SIMULATED Emerald dry run stays on disk: it is regenerable, seeded, with
#   flock /home/sal/duquantumIQM/dq/run/sim.lock nice -n 15 taskset -c 12-15 uv run python scripts/emerald_dryrun.py --clean
# sim/FILES.json lists every file of the full tree with its hashes. Git keeps sim/README.md,
# FILES.json, checks/, ler/, calibration/, architecture/, raw/ and the representative runs below.
# Hardware data (raw/, datasets/, derived/, ler/ at the top level) is never ignored here.
/sim/circuits/
/sim/datasets/*/*
/sim/derived/*/*
!/sim/datasets/E1/ep0_E1_d3_Z_r03_eA/
!/sim/derived/E1/ep0_E1_d3_Z_r03_eA/
!/sim/datasets/E1/b1_E1_d3_Z_r08_eA/
!/sim/derived/E1/b1_E1_d3_Z_r08_eA/
!/sim/datasets/E1/b1_E1_d3_X_r08_eB/
!/sim/derived/E1/b1_E1_d3_X_r08_eB/
!/sim/datasets/E1/b3_E1_d3_Z_r20_eB/
!/sim/derived/E1/b3_E1_d3_Z_r20_eB/
!/sim/datasets/E4/b2_E4_d3_Z_r05_eA_t02000ns/
!/sim/derived/E4/b2_E4_d3_Z_r05_eA_t02000ns/
